    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Represents no value.</para><para>An object of type <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Nothing" kindref="compound">Nothing</ref> can be assigned to any <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Optional" kindref="compound">Optional</ref> object to make it contain nothing.</para><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">Optional&lt;int&gt;<sp/>opt1;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Optional&lt;int&gt;<sp/>opt2(Nothing());</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">Optional&lt;int&gt;<sp/>opt3<sp/>=<sp/>123;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">opt3<sp/>=<sp/>Nothing();</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting></para><para>Anything can be assigned to <ref refid="classSawyer_1_1Nothing" kindref="compound">Nothing</ref> objects and nothing is stored:</para><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">Nothing<sp/>nothing(123);<sp/>//<sp/>still<sp/>empty<sp/>after<sp/>this</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">nothing<sp/>=<sp/>&quot;testing&quot;;<sp/><sp/>//<sp/>still<sp/>empty<sp/>after<sp/>this</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
